## v0.28.0

### CLI exit-code and error-path sweeps (CLI-EXIT-1/2/3, CLI-READBACK-1, CLI-EXIT-4)

- `4efe5674d` — `fix(cli): error paths exit non-zero via abort()` (CLI-EXIT-1).
- `696ff8b31` — `fix(cli): second exit-code sweep — abort() at error();return sites, except-handler AST guard` (CLI-EXIT-2); plus `da60a063d` letting `CLIError` pass `sync_db`'s broad `except`.
- `d36909da1` — `fix(cli): edge.py except-tail error() sites now abort` (CLI-EXIT-3).
- `1356f02d3` — `fix(cli): third exit-code sweep — helper and facade error();return sites abort` (CLI-EXIT-4, ~35 sites, 103 aborts).
- `error()`+`return` sites across ~40 CLI files now exit non-zero
  instead of rc=0 on failure; the corpus AST test guards regression.
  Read-back audit CLI-READBACK-1 (#446) verified `0439846b8` +
  `4efe5674d` with mutation runs — closed as audit, no commits.


### CLI error detail and polish (CLI-ERR-DETAIL-1, CLI-POLISH-2, CLI-POLISH-3)

- `f0cacedd7` — `fix(cli): carry response detail in NetworkError messages`: a refused transaction's RPC 400 detail body is echoed in the CLI error line instead of being hidden (Refs #581).
- `1cc20fc70` — `fix(cli): single refund error line + daemon-down warning without traceback`: removes the empty second error line on escrow refund and the wallet-list daemon-down traceback; shared `run_cli` test helper (Refs #582).
- `52ab53c14` — `fix(cli): no double Error prefix on nested aborts; credential abort carries full text`: ~15 nested sites fixed, the credential abort message in `market/__init__.py` made whole (Refs #590).


## v0.26.0

### CLI-EXIT-1 — error paths exit non-zero instead of printing and returning (CLI; #423)

- 44+ read-only commands exited 0 while printing an error (SP-13), so
  scripted plays and the MCP result field could not tell failure from
  success. The swallowed paths now route through the shared ``abort()``
  helper (printed message unchanged, exit non-zero):
  ``transactions status``, ``explorer`` (all read commands), ``governance``
  (all commands), ``crosschain`` (all commands; the status poll helper keeps
  its transient-tolerant return, now labelled ``warning``), ``gpu discover``
  and the rest of ``gpu_market``, ``monitor alerts/webhooks/campaign/
  sweepers``, ``agent-msg peers``, ``agent discover agents`` (coordinator
  down), ``wallet`` in ``basic.py`` (not-found and error paths), and
  ``coin-requests show/approve/reject/execute/reopen`` refusals.
- Deliberately unchanged: empty-list results (``market list``, alert lists),
  the ``monitor dashboard`` live TUI error rows, ``transactions send``'s
  post-send explorer check, and wallet warnings (daemon fallback, integrity
  mismatch) — those are informational, not failures.
- Tests: ``cli/tests/test_cli_exit_codes.py`` — stubbed-failure invocations
  per command group asserting non-zero exit plus an AST guard that fails on
  any ``error(...)`` immediately followed by ``return`` in the fixed files.

### CLI-HEIGHT-1 — head-reading blockchain commands name their source (CLI; #434)

- ``aitbc blockchain height`` and ``block`` add a ``source`` field to the
  output naming the rpc endpoint the answer came from (default is the node's
  own ``127.0.0.1:8202`` — unchanged).
- ``aitbc blockchain height --db`` reads the local ``chain.db`` directly,
  opened ``mode=ro`` — a heads-equal check that works when the rpc unit is
  down, and never creates the file. Ambiguous or missing stores fail with a
  clear message (``--chain-id`` disambiguates).
- ``aitbc blockchain status`` and ``info`` show a ``Source`` column naming
  the endpoints queried, and accept ``--local`` (this node's rpc) and
  ``--node-url`` (repeatable). ``info`` previously found no chain off the hub
  (empty multichain registry); it now gets the same ``blockchain_rpc_url``
  fallback as ``status``. Defaults are unchanged: plain ``status`` still
  shows the hub view by design.


### CLI-ARRAY-1

- `governance get --proposal-id` and `reputation leaderboard` printed
  "returned a JSON array, not an object" when the service answered a
  bare array. Both callers now use `get_json` and accept either shape:
  `get` selects the matching `proposal_id` from a list (clear not-found
  when absent) and the leaderboard renders the list; dict handling is
  unchanged. Missing-id cases exit non-zero via the shared abort path.


### CLI-AUTHHINT-1

- Commands needing a login printed "No stored credential found for
  'client' in 'default'" and then a raw 401. Credential lookups in
  `ai`/`tee` are now quiet, and a 401 aborts with one line: "No login
  for this environment. Run: aitbc auth login --wallet <name>"
  (shared `LOGIN_HINT` + `is_unauthorized` in `utils/error_handling`).
  `zk health`/`zk circuits` are unchanged: their coordinator endpoints
  answer 401 without a login — auth is genuinely required there.

### CLI-NODEREG-1

- `analytics *`, `blockchain status` and `node chains` printed
  "Authentication failed for node aitbc-primary" on hosts whose
  multichain registry still names the retired aitbc-primary/secondary
  entries on a dead port, even though the local RPC was healthy.
  `load_multichain_config` now always offers the configured
  `blockchain_rpc_url` (default 127.0.0.1:8202) as a `local-rpc`
  fallback node, so a stale registry no longer blinds read commands.


### CLI-LOOPBACK-1

- `gpu discover`/`gpu list-gpus` on customer nodes failed on the
  loopback `gpu_service_url` default with a bare network error. GPU
  failures now append a hint naming the loopback URL and the fix
  (set the service URL — the hub gateway has no `/v1/gpu/` mount).
  Market commands already try the hub before the local service
  (`_candidate_bases`), and `agent-msg peers` honours the explicit
  `--coordinator-url` before the hub-resolved default.

### CLI-POLISH-1

- `brand show` with a missing `AITBC_ACTIVE_PLUGIN` printed a raw
  FileNotFoundError traceback; `_get_brand` now raises a ClickException
  that names the plugin and `aitbc plugin create <name>`.
- `genesis info` printed all-null `genesis_block` fields when the
  genesis file carries no block record; it now reads block 0 from the
  chain DB (read-only) and falls back to a note when it is not sealed.

### CLI-EXIT-2

- Second exit-code sweep (CLI-EXIT-1 residual): ~120 more
