## v0.25.13

### MCP-GROUPS-1 — MCP CLI pivot allow-list derived from the generated group list

- `02f0da5e5` — `aitbc_dispute_*`/`aitbc_energy_*` read tools and the generic
  `run_aitbc_cli`/`read_aitbc_cli`/`list_aitbc_cli_group` pivots answered
  `unknown aitbc group` for ten real CLI groups (`agent-task`, `dispute`,
  `energy`, `eth`, `health`, `liquidity-stake`, `operations`, `service`,
  `stake`, `unstake`): `ALL_AITBC_GROUPS` was a hand-maintained literal
  frozen ten groups behind the generated tool modules (SM-06). The
  generator now emits `aitbc_mcp_cli_tools_generated_groups.py`
  (`GENERATED_AITBC_GROUPS`) in the same `--split-by-group` run — covered
  by the existing `mcp-cli-drift` gate — and the server derives the
  allow-list from it plus a curated-only set (`update`, covered by the
  hand-written `aitbc_update` tool). Destructive-leaf gating is unchanged:
  every mutating leaf in the newly allowed groups was already classified
  by `DESTRUCTIVE_AITBC_SUBCOMMANDS`/`DESTRUCTIVE_AITBC_PATHS`. New tests
  pin three-way consistency (emitted tool modules == group list ⊆
  allow-list == live CLI tree) so a future group cannot silently drift.


## v0.25.12

### Config/CLI: hub-ward URLs resolve locally on the hub; explicit schemes honored

`aitbc.config.hub` detects when the node *is* the hub (`BLOCKCHAIN_MODE=hub`,
or `NODE_ID`/`AITBC_HOSTNAME`/`P2P_NODE_ID` matching the discovery host) and
resolves the hub origin to `HUB_LOCAL_URL` or local nginx `http://127.0.0.1`
— the public name cannot hairpin back there. `hub_origin()`/`hub_service_url()`
now honor explicit `http://` schemes instead of always upgrading to https;
new `normalize_hub_base()`/`is_hub_self()` helpers back every naive call site
(market offers/jobs/escrow/ratings/status/match, network, ipfs, dashboard,
transactions, gpu-onchain, island join). `CLIConfig.hub_blockchain_rpc_url`
derives via `hub_service_url("rpc")` and covers `HUB_P2P_HOST`-only nodes.
Fixes hub-local `market list`/`providers`, `escrow`, `status`, `match` and the
fleet-wide-dead `gpu-onchain`/`island join` hub fallbacks; followers unchanged.


### CLI: aitbc pool-hub on followers used http://{hub}/pool-hub — plain HTTP against a TLS-only edge. Resolved via normalize_hub_base() → https on followers, http://127.0.0.1 on hub. The nginx /pool-hub/ mount already existed; only the scheme was wrong. Also: test_find_service_by_type_and_name now sets API_KEY_STORAGE_PATH → tmp so importing the services router no longer requires /var/lib/aitbc.


### Ops: bridge_wallet_rotation_report analyze() now normalizes withdrawal_by_hash/sell_release_by_hash keys through _norm() — direct callers passing 0x-prefixed/mixed-case eth_tx_hash no longer get unattributed outbound legs (CLI path was already consistent via _load_ledger). ENG-2.


## v0.25.11

### CLI: prepay deposit hardening — zero-wei refuse, malformed chain id, loop close (PREPAY-1b)

Three small guards in `aitbc exchange prepay deposit`, none changing the
accepted path:

- `6f5baac4a` — an `--amount-eth` that floors to 0 wei (e.g. 1e-19) is refused in
  both `--print` and `--send` instead of silently building a zero-value
  transaction.
- `6f5baac4a` — a malformed `eth_chainId` result takes the same clean path as a
  missing one (`chain_id_verified: false` under `--print`; the "cannot
  verify the RPC chain id" abort under `--send`) instead of a raw
  ValueError.
- `6f5baac4a` — `_broadcast_raw` now uses `asyncio.run`, so the broadcast event
  loop is closed after the single send instead of being leaked.



### CLI-5: cheap read-only CLI adds from the 15 Oct gap-log triage

- `dae139a62` — `aitbc wallet inspect --path <file> --field <name>` prints public wallet metadata fields only (address, wallet_id, public_key, type) and refuses private field names (private_key, encrypted, seed, mnemonic, …) with a clear error — never dumps the file.
- `5f7cb0d20` — `aitbc system logs --priority/-p <level>` maps to `journalctl -p` with validation against journal priority names/numbers/ranges; `--severity-pattern` appends a fixed internal application-severity regex (WARN|WARNING|ERROR|CRITICAL|FATAL) that never travels through user input, so the MCP `get_service_logs` blocklist stays untouched; mutually exclusive with `--grep`. MCP exposes `severity_pattern: bool`.
- `65d628b9b` — `exchange_verify.py --db` is now optional: it defaults to the service exchange DB path (EXCHANGE_DATABASE_URL / AITBC_DATA_DIR / /var/lib/aitbc) resolved read-only without creating directories; when AIT-chain args are absent the report names the flags that enable those checks. `aitbc exchange verify --db` follows.
- `cb6dd5ee2` — `GET /v1/bridge/float` (admin-keyed) reports the bridge wallet ETH balance, pending reserve across all three release lanes, and today/rolling-24h release aggregates from new committed-since ledger helpers; CLI gains `aitbc wallet bridge float` and `aitbc wallet bridge status --today/--24h` over the same route, with `--ait-tx-hash` kept as the single-withdrawal lookup.
- `86f52fb03` — sell lane readable without journald: `sell_status_document()` publishes enabled/reason plus non-secret config (key slots as configured booleans) behind `GET /v1/bridge/sell/config-status` (admin-keyed), the `sell_admin status` verb (env-only, runs before the ledger gate), and `aitbc exchange sell_admin status` over the same route.
- item 8 (`exchange order my --wallet` password-free resolution) was already fixed at `983fd1c3c` (CLEAN-1) and is dropped from this batch.


### CLI-6: every `--fee` default tracks `DEFAULT_TX_FEE_AIT`

- REPO-2 (`a0b3dd3c1`) moved `send`/`subscribe`/`batch` onto the shared constant; the remaining `default="0.01"` literals in `aitbc liquidity-stake`, `aitbc wallet send`, and the three `wallet staking` commands now point at `aitbc.utils.units.DEFAULT_TX_FEE_AIT` (0.01 AIT, the CLI-3 decision). The dead `LIQUIDITY_FEE_DEFAULT_AIT` literal in `wallet/staking.py` becomes an alias of the shared constant. Values are unchanged — this is drift-proofing, not a fee change.
- `tests/cli/test_commands_transactions.py::test_batch_default_fee_matches_send` pinned `Decimal("0.001")` — a stale expectation from before `send` moved to the constant; it now asserts the shared constant, so the test passes unweakened. New `tests/cli/test_fee_defaults.py` walks the whole lazy command tree and fails if any `--fee` option defaults to anything else — the drift the batch/send mismatch was.


### CLI-7: mechanical CLI/MCP fixes — ClickException handler, sell names, sell error detail, file-info epilog, MCP logs blocklist

- `c03066a79` — `main()` now catches a plain `click.ClickException` (60 raise sites across 7 files) with `e.show()` + the exception's exit code, so `aitbc http call` non-2xx paths and zero-match `system logs --grep` end in a clean error line instead of a traceback. `Abort`/`UsageError`/`NoArgsIsHelpError` handling is unchanged, and Click's own `Exit` already returns its code under `standalone_mode=False`. This clears the traceback facet of gap rows 17/21; structured non-2xx status/body output for `call_aitbc_http` remains TOOL-1 scope.
- `c03066a79` — `wallet bridge sell` registers its subcommands as `quote`/`lock`/`status`: click had derived `sell-quote`/`sell-lock`/`sell-status` from the function names while every epilog and printed `next` hint named the short forms, so the documented commands did not exist. The generated wallet MCP module re-derives the nested `["bridge","sell","quote|lock|status"]` paths (row 63).
- `c03066a79` — all five sell-lane HTTP error paths (quote POST, lock's quote fetch + nonce fetch, lock submit, status GET) now report `http_error_detail(e)`, so a non-2xx JSON `detail` reaches the error line instead of the bare exception text (row 64).
- `c03066a79` — `aitbc system file-info --help` epilog is generated from the `_FIELD_DENY_*` constants, so the documented refused names cannot drift from the code (row 37).
- `c03066a79` — MCP `get_service_logs` narrows its `since`/`grep` rejection to newline/CR/NUL plus the 200-char limit, mirroring the CLI's own logs validation — `a|b` alternation now reaches `journalctl --grep` (every value is `shlex.quote`d into `--opt=<v>`, so shell metacharacters are inert). The `service` name keeps its strict blocklist since it feeds `journalctl -u` (row 20).


### TOOL-1: MCP/CLI wrapper gaps — nested subcommands, destructive audit, structured http non-2xx, read-only fixes

- `09bd58d10` — `run_aitbc_cli` accepts `subcommand` as `str | list[str]` (a whitespace string is `shlex.split` into argv tokens, so `"exchange node list"` and `["node","list"]` reach the same leaf); `options`/`group_options` accept list values for repeated flags. Closes gap row 28.
- `09bd58d10` — Phase-0 audit of all 543 Click leaves: every mutating or mixed-action leaf is now classified — `DESTRUCTIVE_AITBC_SUBCOMMANDS`/`DESTRUCTIVE_AITBC_PATHS` gained `set-payout`, `sell lock|quote`, `sync`, `sweep`, `rekey`, `http call`, `monitor alerts|webhooks`, `deploy deploy-brand`, `migrate`, and bare top-level `start|stop|restart|stake|update`. A structural test walks the command tree and fails when a handler carrying mutation signals is unclassified; `read_aitbc_cli` rejects destructive paths for nested/list forms (previously `http call` was reachable through the read-only tool).
- `09bd58d10` — `aitbc http call` gains repeatable `--expect-status N`: an expected non-2xx prints `{"status": N, "detail": …}` and exits 0; other non-2xx exits non-zero with one line (`HTTP <status> from <service>/<path>: <detail>`). `RateLimitError`/`CircuitBreakerOpenError` (re-raised unwrapped by the client) render as ClickExceptions. Exposed on MCP `call_aitbc_http` as `expect_status`. Closes the row-17 remainder; deterministic 4xx are already not retried (`retry_policy.py` raises 4xx immediately), no client change needed.
- `09bd58d10` — `system logs --grep`: journalctl rc=1 with "-- No entries --" is success (the line is printed); every other non-zero exit stays an error. Closes row 21.
- `09bd58d10` — `monitor campaigns` (and `campaign_stats`) compute expired/ended status in memory: listing no longer creates or rewrites `~/.aitbc/campaigns/campaigns.json`, so the MCP read-only annotation is now true. Closes row 33.
- `09bd58d10` — `generate_mcp_cli_tools.py`: `("dispute","file")` added to `FORCE_DESTRUCTIVE_PATHS` — its leaf token `file` landed in the safe-token set and the generated `aitbc_dispute_file` was emitted read-only while filing disputes; regenerated modules gate it behind dry_run+confirm. Row 23 re-run: connected MCP server still predates the `= None` optional-param fix (`4b214fdb2`) — 12 "Field required" errors; row stays open.


### MSG-CLI-WAIT
- `messaging send`/action commands: the default `--wait` seal poll moved off the generic `/rpc/transaction/{hash}` route (which 404s for MESSAGE txs even sealed — tripped the client circuit breaker live in MSG-3d) onto messaging read routes via plain `requests`: posts/replies detected at `/rpc/messaging/messages/{hash}`, actions via the topic moderation `actions` list. Timeout now prints a "submitted, verify with …" hint and exits 0; a silent RPC is distinguished from a 404 storm. 5 new tests in `test_messaging_wait.py`. MCP messaging wrappers regenerated (help text only).


### MSG-CLI-WAIT (fix 2)
- vote/mod_grant/mod_revoke never appear in the moderation `actions` list, so the fix-1 wait polled the full timeout and hinted the wrong route. They now detect by *state* — vote via the target's `/votes` route (signer+value), grant/revoke via the topic `moderators` list — and report "reads as expected" rather than "sealed". A pre-send probe reports "already reads as expected" instead of claiming a seal when state predates submission; unknown kinds print a verify-hint immediately without waiting. 8 new tests (per-kind routes, wrong-value/still-present keep polling, unknown kind, pre-send probe, command-level pre-match).


### MSG-CLI-WAITc
- Retract (`vote` value 0): matched by the signer's *absence* from the target's standing votes ("vote retracted — signer absent"), so it no longer burns the full --wait-timeout; a retract with no standing vote is pre-matched and reports "nothing to retract" instead of claiming a seal.
- Non-moderator moderation sends: `_presend_expectations` reads the topic moderators once before submit; a non-moderator signer gets "submitted; recorded but not effective for a non-moderator" at once — no 180 s hash wait (the `actions` list only ever holds moderator-signed rows). Applies to all eight moderator-gated kinds.
- Moderation hash waits now cap at 30 s when the `actions` list reads at its 100-entry cap (a fresh hash can have scrolled out). `--wait` help names each detection route. 6 new tests; `_wait_confirmed`/`_poll_read` helpers keep C901 flat.


### MSG-CLI-HASH-1
- fix(cli): all `aitbc messaging` commands accept bare or 0x-prefixed 64-hex tx hashes — normalized once to bare at parse; read routes use the 0x-prefixed form


### CLI-SENDER-1 — sender/recipient filters on /rpc/transactions + aitbc transactions search

- `/rpc/transactions` accepts `sender` and `recipient` parameters —
  same spelling handling as `address` (checksum + lowercase), combinable;
  all supplied filters hold. `address` semantics unchanged.
- `aitbc transactions search` now works over RPC (was explorer-only):
  `--sender`, `--recipient`, `--address` (at least one required),
  `--rpc-url`. The explorer path refuses `--sender/--recipient` with a
  clear message rather than returning either-side rows.
